Fixed a REST API information-disclosure issue where the `?depth=N` query parameter exposed the full detail of related objects that the requesting user did not have permission to view. Related objects that the user cannot view are now rendered in a brief `{id, object_type, url, display}` form instead of full detail. The `display` value is included for parity with the UI, where a related object's display value is visible without requiring full view permission on that object. Additionally, the Notes REST API now enforces `view` permission on the object a note is being assigned to on write (POST/PATCH), consistent with other object references.
